FILE: vUX-component.js
FEATURE: skeleton-module
DATE: 2026-10-05
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'timeline-list-verification' (uncommitted at the time)

REASON
Bug found while building the Skeleton example. Component.sync() wrapped a newly
built row in its public Instance only inside the onMount callback, and only when
config.onMount was set. With no onMount:
  - sync() returned an array of undefined for every new row, because it reads
    result.order[x].instance;
  - instances() and destroyAll() skip entries without an instance, so
    destroyAll() left every synced row in the page.
The Skeleton playground switches templates with destroyAll() and showed both
lists at once. The Component example always sets onMount, which is why the bug
had not shown. The Instance is now always made. onMount is still called
exactly once per new row, with the same object.


================================================================================
CHANGE 1
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
            onMount: function(entry){ if (onMount != null) onMount(makeInstance(entry)); },

NEW_SECTION
            //The Instance is made whether or not onMount is set: sync()'s return value,
            //instances() and destroyAll() all reach a row through entry.instance.
            onMount: function(entry){ var instance = makeInstance(entry); if (onMount != null) onMount(instance); },
